  "title": "India’s Election Commission Faces Controversy Over SIR Revisions and Protests",
  "summary": "The Election Commission of India faced criticism over its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders following allegations of procedural issues. Congress demanded immediate action to address concerns, including the suspension of a controversial SIR exercise, while the Commission defended its processes and claimed the changes to electoral rolls were upheld by legal standards.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Election Commission of India has faced allegations of procedural issues with its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Congress demanded immediate action to address the ongoing SIR exercise and the allegations of disenfranchisement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Commission defended its processes and claims that changes to electoral rolls and voter lists were upheld by the Supreme Court.",
      "confidence": 0.95
